WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.400
AI detection tools estimate whether media may be synthetic or manipulated.

00:00:04.400 --> 00:00:09.120
They can analyze patterns in pixels, frames, audio, compression, or model-specific traces.

00:00:09.120 --> 00:00:12.720
Their output should be treated as one analytical input, not final proof.

00:00:12.720 --> 00:00:16.000
A false positive occurs when genuine or benign media is flagged.

00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:20.230
A false negative occurs when synthetic or manipulated media is missed.

00:00:20.230 --> 00:00:24.200
Consequences can be serious, especially when a result affects reputation, employment,

00:00:24.200 --> 00:00:26.806
safety, legal action, or public reporting.

00:00:26.806 --> 00:00:30.030
Detection performance changes as generation models, editing pipelines,

00:00:30.030 --> 00:00:31.150
and platforms change.

00:00:31.150 --> 00:00:34.920
A detector trained on older examples may not recognize new systems.

00:00:34.920 --> 00:00:38.915
Model drift and limited evaluation data can make a published accuracy number misleading

00:00:38.915 --> 00:00:40.810
for a specific case.

00:00:40.810 --> 00:00:44.050
Platform processing can resize, recompress, filter, or transcode media,

00:00:44.050 --> 00:00:46.282
altering the signals a detector uses.

00:00:46.282 --> 00:00:47.790
Cropping, screenshots, noise,

00:00:47.790 --> 00:00:51.790
and adversarial changes can also shift scores without changing the underlying claim.

00:00:51.790 --> 00:00:53.155
Use multiple forms of evidence.

00:00:53.155 --> 00:00:58.200
Review provenance, source history, visual and audio observations, metadata, timeline,

00:00:58.200 --> 00:00:59.440
and independent corroboration.

00:00:59.440 --> 00:01:00.720
If several detectors agree,

00:01:00.720 --> 00:01:04.200
ask whether they share training assumptions or failure modes before calling them

00:01:04.200 --> 00:01:04.880
independent.

00:01:04.880 --> 00:01:08.880
Report the tool, version, input, result, limitations, and interpretation.

00:01:08.880 --> 00:01:10.320
A score is not a verdict.

00:01:10.320 --> 00:01:13.680
Human analysis remains essential for understanding the claim, context,

00:01:13.680 --> 00:01:16.790
alternative explanations, and potential harm of an incorrect label.
